{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "First Day of Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "From Scratch"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "judgment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "making a decision about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  People may make judgments based on what you wear in the first few weeks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about what to do on your first day at work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dress "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to choose and wear clothes for a particular situation, like work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The next thing is you must dress professionally."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "established"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "set; created; made up"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People don't have an established idea of your abilities yet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "loyalty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dedication towards a person or a group"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You will show loyalty to your co-workers by sharing credit with the team."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to share credit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say that a situation is good because another person or group worked hard "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's important to share credit with all the people who work on a team."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le06ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals to Express True, Untrue Events in the Present"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The modals <span class=\"italic\">may, might, could</span> and<span class=\"italic\"> will</span> are usually used to talk about possibility in the future (predicting).<br/><br/>  You can also use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may, might, could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to say whether you think something is <span class=\"underline\">true or likely in the present</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You put the modal before the main verb. It is also possible to add <span class=\"italic\">not </span> to the modal to talk about things you believe to be untrue.<br/><br/>  For example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">might</span> be right. </span>(It's likely)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">may</span> have a point there.</span> (It's not impossible)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">That <span class=\"strong\">could</span> be true.</span> (It's not impossible)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">That'<span class=\"strong\">ll</span> be my sister on the phone.</span> (I'm quite sure)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Beth'<span class=\"strong\">ll</span> be arriving in Montreal about now.</span>(It's probable)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> be there already!</span> (I don't believe she is)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since people don't have an established idea of your abilities yet, they may make judgments based on what you wear in the first few weeks."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You will show loyalty to your co-workers by sharing credit with the team."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Five Tips to Make a Great First Impression at Work - What is Necessary and Not Necessary"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " First impressions are important. When you meet someone, it is crucial that you present yourself in the best way possible, both in how you act and what you look like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are five tips to keep in mind if you want to make a great first impression on your first day at a new job:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li>You <span class=\"strong\">need to have</span> a positive attitude. </li><li>You <span class=\"strong\">mustn't bring</span> non-work problems to the office.</li><li>You <span class=\"strong\">must dress</span> professionally. </li><li>You <span class=\"strong\">need to figure out</span> what is going on, both officially and unofficially.</li><li>You <span class=\"strong\">must listen</span> carefully to what people say or don't say, and be observant.</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Follow these guidelines to make the best first impression possible!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice the use of the <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs </span><span class=\"italic\">must, mustn't, need and needn't</span>. You use these modals to express necessity and what is not necessary. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We needn't feel stressed. </span>(It is not necessary for us to feel stressed)"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of the ways of making a good impression that are mentioned in this lesson."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss these suggestions, and try to think of others."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online. Try to find a total of 6 - 10 <span class=\"strong\">different</span> suggestions to make a good impression at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the suggestions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In your own words, explain why each one is important."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Add 1 - 2 things you should <span class=\"strong\">avoid</span> (not do) to your list."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your list to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about ways to make a good impression at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss making a good impression at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write suggestions for making a good impression."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express necessity, duty and advice. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express true, untrue, and possible events. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange opinions about  events and experiences in various time frames.   "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think first impressions are important?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How can you make a good first impression at work?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How can you make a bad first impression?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Here's how to make a good impression!"}]